# .github/CODEOWNERS — which paths pull a named human into the review.
#
# This file requests reviewers. It does NOT block a merge on its own: enforcement
# requires a repository ruleset that opts in to code-owner review, and this
# repository has no ruleset at all today (the rulesets and branch-protection APIs
# both return HTTP 403 "Upgrade to GitHub Pro or make this repository public",
# verified 2026-08-07). So this file is the reviewer routing described in
# CONTRIBUTING.md "Review, and what requires a human reviewer", and the rule it
# encodes becomes enforceable the moment a ruleset can exist.
#
# Keep it narrow. A CODEOWNERS entry on every path assigns one person to every
# pull request, which is how a review requirement decays into a rubber stamp.

# --- Security-sensitive: cryptography, identity, authorization, publication ----
# A change here always carries a named human security reviewer. An autonomous
# lane never merges one on its own authority.
/crates/mesh-crypto/          @idosams
/crates/mesh-approval/        @idosams
/crates/mesh-policy/          @idosams
/tests/authorization/         @idosams

# --- The protocol -------------------------------------------------------------
# A protocol schema and its implementation are never changed in one unsupervised
# run; the second pair of eyes is the mechanism.
/protocol/                    @idosams
/crates/mesh-sync-protocol/   @idosams
/crates/mesh-types/           @idosams

# --- Licensing and the edition boundary ---------------------------------------
# Adding a licence to the allow-list is a decision, never a local edit.
/LICENSE                      @idosams
/deny.toml                    @idosams
/docs/launch/                 @idosams
/tools/program/license-check.mjs  @idosams

# --- The gate suite and CI definition -----------------------------------------
# A change that makes a gate quieter is reviewed as a policy change.
/.github/                     @idosams
/tools/program/               @idosams

# --- Repository governance ----------------------------------------------------
/CLAUDE.md                    @idosams
/.claude/                     @idosams
